SM(271,{"n":"Genesis 43-45","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Genesis 43-45.mp3","d":2742.5,"s":[[0.24,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.96,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in Biblical Studies, and is an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[21.44,"Chapter 43. Now the famine was severe in the land."],[26.72,"So when it came to pass when they had eaten the grain they brought from Egypt, their father said to them, Go back and buy us a little food."],[33.36,"They've left Simeon there."],[37.76,"All this time."],[38.56,"Remember, this is a seven-year famine."],[42.0,"So that was Jacob's decision."],[44.24,"Bye, Simeon. That was his decision."],[50.28,"But now they're out of food again."],[51.88,"Now everybody's starving to death."],[53.4,"The animals are starving to death."],[54.6,"They're going to starve to death."],[55.97,"So now he says, go back and get some food."],[59.77,"But Judah spoke to him saying, the man solemnly warned us, saying, You shall not see my face unless your brother is with you."],[67.93,"If you send our brother with us, we will go down and buy you food."],[71.77,"But if you will not send him, we will not go down."],[74.65,"For the man said to us, You shall not see my face unless your brother is with you."],[79.39,"So Judah's like, I'm not going back there without Benjamin, because he will kill us."],[89.6,"And kind of implied, like, I know you don't care, Dad."],[95.68,"But I do."],[98.49,"So I'm not going unless you let Benjamin come with us."],[103.25,"And Israel said, This is Israel, the person, Jacob, Why did you deal so wrongfully with me as to tell the man whether you had yet another brother?"],[116.85,"Yeah. Yeah. Why'd you even tell him you had another brother?"],[127.41,"But they said the man asked us pointedly about ourselves and our family, saying, Is your father still alive?"],[133.17,"Have you another brother?"],[134.85,"Thus we replied to him according to these words."],[137.81,"Could we possibly have known he would say, Bring your brother down?"],[141.91,"They're like, listen, he asked us, why would we have thought he was going to demand to see our younger brother?"],[149.15,"Like, why? So is there a reason it's shifted from saying Jacob to Israel now at this point?"],[159.95,"Or does that like is that just in uh part of the English translation?"],[165.07,"Well, that is part of the English translation, but also, he has he has both names."],[171.91,"And usually when they're calling him Israel."],[175.21,"Yeah, with Abraham, when his name gets changed, he's just Abraham thereafter."],[178.89,"Whereas in this story, it goes back and forth."],[182.11,"And usually when when it's referring to him as Israel, it's trying to make the point."],[189.23,"Remember, this is the Genesis is the prologue to the Torah"],[193.59,"It's trying to make a point about the people, his descendants as a whole."],[200.41,"That he is because remember, that's that's how he gets named."],[204.17,"He gets named after the wrestling match."],[207.14,"The one who struggles with God."],[209.46,"And that's kind of the character of Israel going forward in the Torah."],[214.39,"And so the same kind of thing is likely true here."],[221.56,"And here, as you mentioned earlier, this contrast with Abraham."],[226.83,"Now he's withholding from God the thing that's precious to him."],[236.41,"The thing that's most precious, he's withholding, which is the opposite of Abraham."],[241.14,"Who the most precious thing he had, he was willing to offer to God."],[246.12,"Now it's this withholding."],[249.1,"And this bickering and this infighting between even the tribes."],[254.72,"And specifically, who is it who's been talking to him?"],[258.72,"Judah. So there is this enmity here between Judah and Israel that sort of prefigures even what will happen when the when the kingdoms, when the kingdoms split."],[274.7,"Where and where it's Judah is the one who's talking sense and speaking the truth, and Israel is the one who's sort of withholding, and right."],[284.46,"So it's kind of it's kind of like a just reemphasizing the wrestling, the wrestling aspect."],[292.78,"Yeah. Kind of saying to his descendants who read this, look, this is where you come from."],[298.22,"Yeah. You are the way you are."],[300.3,"Apple doesn't fall far from the tree."],[302.06,"Yeah. Yeah. Okay."],[304.46,"Then Judah said to Israel, his father, send the lad with me, and we will arise and go, that we may live and not die, both we and you, and all we have."],[314.59,"So he says, Look, trust me."],[315.95,"I will take him, send him with me"],[317.83,"This uh Reuben had tried the same thing."],[319.75,"He's like, trust Jesus, trust me."],[322.87,"He's like, if I don't take him, we all die."],[328.47,"You die, he dies, we die."],[332.55,"The whole family dies of starvation."],[334.65,"Because the animals all die."],[337.02,"So I know you don't want to risk his life, but he's gonna die of starvation too if we don't go."],[344.92,"So this is what we need to do."],[349.8,"Verse nine, I myself will be surety for him."],[353.24,"From my hand you shall require him."],[355.4,"If I do not bring him back to you and set him before you, then let me bear the blame all my days."],[360.2,"For if we had not lingered, surely by now we would have returned this second time"],[366.88,"So he adds that at the end."],[369.54,"If you had just let us take him back originally, we wouldn't be having this problem."],[377.18,"Verse 11. Then their father Israel said to them, If it must be so, then do this."],[383.18,"Take some of the best fruits of the land in your vessels, and carry down a present for the man, a little balm and a little honey, spices and myrrh, pistachio nuts and almonds."],[395.18,"Take double money in your hand and take back in your hand the money returned in the mouth of your sacks."],[400.62,"Perhaps it was an oversight."],[402.9,"Okay. So he says, just say, hey, there was a mistake."],[407.78,"We got our money back."],[408.9,"So give him that money, plus a new batch of money for more grain."],[412.58,"And also just give him a gift over and above that."],[415.8,"Of the stuff we have."],[417.62,"You notice that's not like really foodstuffs, like that you could feed flocks and herds."],[423.24,"But we've still got you've got tree resin."],[425.4,"We got some."],[427.48,"So bring that."],[428.7,"So ingratiate yourselves."],[430.59,"And and return all that money."],[433.47,"Take your brother also, and arise, go back to the man."],[439.39,"May God give you grace before the man that he may release your other brother and Benjamin."],[444.91,"Oh, what was his name?"],[446.03,"Oh, yeah, Simeon."],[446.91,"Notice what his strategy is"],[450.07,"If I am bereaved, I am bereaved."],[454.31,"You remember the last time he used this strategy?"],[457.27,"He was meeting Esau."],[458.47,"Remember? He said all the gifts."],[460.47,"And he said all the people before they're in a famine, so he doesn't have so much with the gifts."],[465.13,"But he's trying the same tactic."],[467.55,"Okay, do everything you can to ingratiate yourself to this guy."],[472.05,"But he does see the sense of what Judah is saying."],[474.45,"Like, yeah, if we don't at least try this, we're all dead."],[477.65,"Benjamin included. So this is a risk we have to take."],[481.99,"So the men took that present and Benjamin, and they took double money in their hand, and arose and went down to Egypt, and they stood before Joseph."],[490.35,"When Joseph saw Benjamin, his brother by the same mother with them, he said to the steward of his house, take these men to my home and slaughter an animal and make ready, for these men will dine with me at noon."],[502.75,"Then the man did as Joseph ordered, and the man brought the men into Joseph's house."],[532.19,"Joseph had to know what his dad was like."],[535.51,"Joseph had to know with Joseph gone, Benjamin would be the favorite."],[542.07,"And the youngest son being the favorite, almost got him killed."],[547.63,"Very close to got him killed."],[550.51,"So he had every reason to think killed Benjamin too."],[554.43,"They may have done something to him too."],[558.83,"So he wanted to see him intact."],[563.07,"And when he saw he was intact, then he could rightly conclude what?"],[568.75,"Well, my dad may not have changed, but that is something had changed with his brothers."],[576.29,"Something had changed with his brothers."],[578.49,"He didn't want revenge against his brothers, as it was."],[582.78,"But now. When people are repentant, that helps a lot with forgiveness."],[590.41,"He had already forgiven them."],[593.21,"Which is saying something."],[597.45,"We made kind of a big deal about Esau's forgiveness of his brother Jacob."],[603.41,"But like, Jacob didn't literally try to murder Esau."],[607.49,"I'd have to be talked out of it."],[610.3,"Like, didn't have Esau sol sold into slavery."],[615.2,"Esau didn't spend years in prison in a hole."],[620.52,"Like, if anybody had reason not to forgive, Joseph."],[629.13,"If anybody has had a reason to want revenge, it would be Joseph."],[636.09,"Before we started, we mentioned the movie Gladiator."],[641.77,"It's a classic revenge story."],[644.63,"Like, how many of our films, how many, how many plays, going all the way back to Greek tragedies, are revenge stories."],[652.87,"Someone gets wronged in a manner like Joseph and goes out and wreaks horrible revenge."],[659.59,"And we watch something like that, and that's a satisfying conclusion to us when they get their revenge."],[663.35,"That's not at all what we're presented with here"],[670.07,"Satisfying conclusions of the book of Genesis are when Jacob and Esau are reconciled."],[677.01,"It's when Isaac and Ishmael bury their father together."],[682.69,"And it's Joseph forgiving his brothers."],[685.01,"They haven't asked forgiveness yet."],[688.69,"They don't know who he is."],[690.37,"They haven't asked for forgiveness."],[694.29,"But he's already forgiven them."],[695.57,"He couldn't even keep them all imprisoned."],[699.86,"For more than three days."],[704.5,"And this is another part of that pattern."],[705.06,"is another part of that pattern. This"],[712.78,"Because Christ's resurrection does not go out for revenge."],[719.74,"He doesn't go out for revenge against the people of Jerusalem."],[723.9,"He doesn't go out for revenge against the Romans."],[730.22,"He rises bringing forgiveness."],[734.22,"This is what Hebrews is talking about."],[736.14,"If you remember back to when we went through Hebrews, and talked about the blood of Christ is the blood that speaks a better word than that of Abel."],[743.66,"So remember what Abel's blood after his brother murdered him, called out from the ground for justice."],[750.78,"Christ's blood doesn't."],[751.42,"Calls out for forgiveness"],[758.58,"Joseph is part of here in Genesis establishing that pattern."],[763.14,"Jacob and Esau is reconciliation."],[765.22,"Isaac and Ishmael's reconciliation."],[768.15,"So this idea of forgiveness, of reconciliation between people and with God is not a New Testament thing."],[780.31,"Again, it's not mean, angry God of vengeance in the Old Testament."],[786.55,"Going around punishing everybody for their sins, and then Jesus comes and oh, now we have forgiveness."],[791.51,"Forgiveness and reconciliation is the earliest pattern we have in the Bible in terms of how things end."],[800.37,"Of what the good ending is."],[805.17,"Not vengeance. Verse 18."],[811.57,"Now the men, Joseph's brothers, were afraid because they were brought into Joseph's house."],[818.21,"So he hasn't said anything to them why."],[820.61,"They just all get led into his house."],[823.22,"We have every reason to believe that this would just be some gigantic, huge, massive."],[828.18,"By the standards of the day, yes."],[830.1,"This is a palatial, yes, a boat."],[834.06,"And they said, It is because of the money returned to our sacks the first time that we are brought here to make a case against us and fall upon us to take us as slaves with our donkeys."],[845.68,"So they say, Oh, they're gonna enslave us."],[848.24,"That's why we're being brought here."],[850.02,"Because they think we stole the we stole the grain last time, and so they're gonna enslave us as punishment."],[858.26,"Verse 19, when they drew near to the steward of Joseph's house, they talked with him at the door of the house, saying, We entreat you, my lord, we indeed came down the first time to buy food."],[868.42,"But it happened when we came to the encampment, that we opened our sacks, and there to our surprise, each man's money was in the mouth of his sack, our money in full weight."],[877.78,"So we have brought it back in our hand."],[879.62,"So notice the weight."],[881.16,"Because it's not uh coins, yeah."],[883.32,"And we have brought down other money in our hands to buy food"],[889.36,"We do not know who put the money in our sacks."],[892.32,"So as they're being brought to the house, they see the steward, sort of the guy who's in charge of running the household stuff, and they're like, Oh, hey, by the way, uh, that whole money thing was a misunderstanding."],[902.48,"Uh, we've got it to give back to you, we've got more money besides, it's all good."],[906.32,"Uh, don't enslave us, maybe."],[912.56,"But he said, Mercy be on you, do not be afraid."],[915.6,"Your God and the God of your father has given you treasure in your sacks, and I am receiving your genuine money as full payment."],[922.96,"Then he brought Simeon out to them."],[926.8,"So now they're confused."],[927.84,"Verse 24 Yeah."],[932.04,"So the man brought the men into Joseph's house and gave them water, and they washed their feet, and he gave their donkeys feed."],[939.32,"Then they made the present ready for Joseph's coming at noon, for they heard he would eat bread there."],[945.66,"So like, oh, he's coming, he's coming here to eat."],[948.14,"Okay, well, get the presents and stuff we got him."],[950.38,"Let's, you know, ingratiate ourselves."],[955.58,"Thus, when Joseph came home, they brought the present in their hand to him in the house and bowed down before him to the earth."],[961.9,"Then he asked him about their well being and said, Is your father well?"],[965.1,"The old man of whom you spoke, is he still alive?"],[968.38,"So they answered, Your servant our father is in good health, he is still alive."],[973.94,"Then he said, Blessed be that man in God, and they bowed their heads down and prostrated themselves."],[980.1,"So they do it again."],[983.78,"By the way, they're not worshiping Joseph."],[987.3,"Just adding that as a comment, bowing down and prostrating yourself."],[993.22,"Does not mean you're worshiping something."],[996.9,"Don't know who needs to hear that."],[998.58,"You might have ideas."],[1010.42,"So he said, May God grant you mercy, my son."],[1013.46,"Now his heart yearned for his brother, so Joseph made haste and sought somewhere to weep."],[1018.62,"Then he went into his inner chamber and wept there."],[1022.06,"He then washed his face and came out, and he composed himself and said, Serve the bread."],[1026.62,"So Joseph doesn't have a super good poker face."],[1029.95,"He has to kind of keep taking these breaks and sort of uh hiding a little bit, letting it out, and then you know, gets himself back together and comes back out."],[1043.47,"So they set him a place by himself, and them by themselves, and the Egyptians who ate with him by themselves?"],[1049.99,"Because the Egyptians could not eat food with the Hebrews, for that is an abomination to the Egyptians."],[1056.59,"So where were we talked about?"],[1060.11,"These people are filthy."],[1062.05,"The whole hygiene thing."],[1063.81,"So they wouldn't sit with them, they wouldn't sit next to them, they wouldn't have anything to do with them."],[1067.41,"So Joseph kind of has his own table, like up at the head, and then his brothers are at this other table, and the Egyptians who are part of Joseph's retinue right now."],[1077.01,"So they won't the Egyptians won't eat with Joseph because he's from these people, even though he's not."],[1082.13,"No, Joseph is at the head table because he's just big position."],[1086.05,"Yeah, he's the big cheese."],[1087.73,"Yeah. Yeah. Because he's following all the Joseph's following all the hygiene roles."],[1092.53,"Verse 33. Now they sat before him, the firstborn according to his birthright, and the youngest according to his youth."],[1098.69,"And the men looked in astonishment at one another."],[1101.81,"Then he took servings to them from before him, but Benjamin's serving was five times as much as any of theirs."],[1107.01,"s. So now he' kind of messing with them a little"],[1107.69,"So they drank and were merry with him."],[1114.23,"Because he has them seated at the table, and he seats them in the correct order from oldest to youngest."],[1119.19,"So they're kind of going."],[1135.27,"So if you've got a guy who's the official, the food would be brought out of the kitchen to him."],[1142.11,"And he would take what he wanted, and then he would send food as he saw fit to the other tables."],[1149.63,"So the idea is normally you would expect like the Egyptians to get that, and these people might, you know, would then get what was left after they ate."],[1161.2,"There was sort of a descending order."],[1165.25,"Um sending stuff directly from his table to the brothers."],[1171.81,"That's why it points that out."],[1173.09,"That that would be weird."],[1174.53,"And then even weirder, he's specifically having stuff sent to Benjamin to the youngest brother, which would be a little odd."],[1183.99,"So this was true, by the way, in families, too."],[1188.57,"So the food would get brought to the head of the household, father."],[1194.07,"So like Jacob."],[1196.24,"Jacob would take what he wanted, then it would get sent to firstborn son, all the way down through the sons, then mom, then daughters."],[1208.02,"Is how that was typically done."],[1210.34,"We could expect that probably in Jacob's house it was leapfrogging like him, Joseph."],[1218.74,"That was part of the problem."],[1223.62,"Yeah. But these these kids so these kind of hierarchies were reinforced constantly."],[1230.02,"I mean, every time they ate."],[1233.32,"Every time at all times."],[1234.84,"So this wasn't just like like fav.oritism, in general"],[1238.08,"Like he gave him a gift to everyone, everybody knows he's the favorite."],[1241.7,"Like my sisters know I'm the favorite."],[1243.38,"It drives them nuts, but you know, it's not reinforced continuously."],[1248.04,"Just every once in a while comes out."],[1250.44,"But the uh, but this is this is a hierarchy that's constantly reinforced."],[1257.48,"So this is part of where the brothers' rage came from earlier, is that this was kind of thrown in their face day in and day out, over and over again."],[1268.12,"This wasn't being done the way it should be."],[1272.16,"Um, to accentuate that."],[1274.42,"And so, but now they see this weird thing happening here."],[1278.26,"But since we heard they're making merry, they're probably getting drunk, and so it just seems kind of weird."],[1284.24,"Why did he want to see our Yuga's brother so bad?"],[1286.32,"Why is he spoiling him now?"],[1287.52,"Huh, that's weird."],[1288.96,"Isn't he kind of reestablishing order too?"],[1291.84,"Like by lining them up, isn't Joseph like fixing."],[1297.04,"Yeah, in a way, yeah, yeah, yeah."],[1300.08,"But then he's violating it by giving all his own."],[1302.49,"Yeah. So that's it's confusing."],[1304.97,"I feel like that's more like a he's giving them a subtle clue that he knows what's going on."],[1309.91,"But he's also, why is he giving so much extra to Benjamin?"],[1313.43,"To see if they're gonna react."],[1314.63,"To see how they're gonna react."],[1316.2,"He's not done."],[1316.84,"right He still hasn't told them who he is, he's still trying to see what's going on and if anything's changed."],[1321.66,"And so this is a test"],[1323.46,"They're not getting angry their son."],[1327.13,"Is one of are they gonna get angry?"],[1329.05,"Are they going to object that he's the youngest son?"],[1332.19,"Chapter 44. Now Joseph commanded the steward of the house, saying, Fill the men's sacks with food, as much as they can carry, and put each man's money in the mouth of the sack."],[1343.79,"Also put my cup, the silver cup, in the mouth of the sack of the youngest and his grain money."],[1350.51,"So he did according to the word Joseph had spoken."],[1354.51,"So he says, Do what you did last time, give them their money back."],[1358.36,"He says, and by the way, the solid silver cup I have, very valuable object."],[1363.96,"From my house where they all just were eating and drinking"],[1368.46,"Take that and put it in the youngest son's bag."],[1375.66,"Verse three. As soon as the morning dawned, the men were sent away, they and their donkeys."],[1380.06,"When they had gone out of the city and were not yet far off, Joseph said to his steward, Get up, follow the men, and when you overtake them, say to them, Why have you repaid evil for good?"],[1390.22,"Why have you stolen my silver cup?"],[1392.78,"Is not this the cup from which my lord drinks, and with which he indeed practices divination?"],[1398.38,"You have done evil in so doing."],[1401.26,"Okay So, the divination thing, why does he throw that in there?"],[1405.58,"Well, we're trying to keep up the roost that this is an Egyptian guy."],[1410.03,"And so that was after you drink wine, you look at the dregs."],[1414.85,"Just like people can read tea leaves."],[1416.37,"You can read the dregs of the wine to get omens and stuff."],[1418.87,"So we're trying to read from oh, this he's a real Egyptian Egyptian."],[1422.16,"Like, this is a but so this is the cup."],[1424.42,"So he says, Go chase him down."],[1426.34,"Say, How dare you steal the silver cup?"],[1436.15,"Verse 6. So he overtook them and he spoke to them these same words, but they said to him, Why does my lord say these words?"],[1442.31,"Far be it from us that your servants should do such a thing."],[1445.75,"Look, we brought back to you from the land of Canaan the money we found in the mouth of our sacks."],[1450.31,"How then could we steal silver or gold from your Lord's house?"],[1454.19,"They're like, Don't you remember when we found the money?"],[1456.67,"We brought it back."],[1458.29,"We're clearly not trying to steal from you."],[1460.37,"If we were dishonest, we wouldn't have brought it back."],[1463.09,"With whomever of your servants it is found, let him die, and we also will be my lord's servants."],[1469.11,"So they're so sure nobody did this."],[1471.91,"They're like, hey, if you find it somewhere in our little caravan here, whoever stole it, you can execute them."],[1478.79,"And does that mean that we will be your slaves now?"],[1482.07,"No, say we'll, we'll we won't object."],[1486.07,"Okay. We'll. Verse 10."],[1490.09,"Then he replied, Now, as you say, so it will be."],[1493.05,"He with whom it is found shall be my servant, and you shall be blameless."],[1493.93,"So he says, I'm not going to kill him"],[1499.72,"But I'm going to take him back, whoever it is, back to be a slave."],[1505.48,"For theft. Because that's why they thought they were going to be enslaved."],[1508.63,"That was the penalty in Egypt at this time for theft, is you would be enslaved for a period of time to work off the value of what you stole."],[1518.81,"However, that was assessed."],[1520.17,"In this case, that'd be a long time."],[1528.49,"Verse 11. Then each man speedily let down his sack to the ground, and each opened his sack."],[1533.45,"So he searched the oldest and left off with the youngest, and the cup was found in Benjamin's sack."],[1536.81,"Then they tore their clothes, and each man loaded his donkey and returned to the city"],[1544.21,"They're like, ah!"],[1548.03,"Like, we can't go back to our dad."],[1551.07,"Like the one who we couldn't lose."],[1556.96,"So notice they go back to the city."],[1558.32,"They go back to Egypt."],[1559.52,"They don't go back to uh back to their dad."],[1563.52,"Because they're like, we gotta figure this out."],[1565.54,"We can't go back to their dad without Benjamin."],[1569.86,"So Judah and his brothers came to Joseph's house, and he was still there, and they fell before him on the ground."],[1576.58,"Thus Joseph said to them, What is this thing you have done?"],[1580.06,"Did you not know that such a man as I can certainly practice divination?"],[1587.18,"Then Judah said, What shall we say to my lord?"],[1589.9,"What shall we speak, or how shall we clear ourselves?"],[1592.62,"God has found out the wrongdoing of your servants."],[1595.18,"Here we are, my lord's slaves, both we and he also with whom the cup was found."],[1601.58,"But Joseph said, Far be it from me that I should do so."],[1604.86,"The man in whose hand the cup was found, he shall be my servant."],[1608.14,"And as for you, go up in peace to your father."],[1611.35,"So he says, Oh, I'm just taking the one who right, they come and say, No, no, no, just take us."],[1618.36,"Take us as slaves."],[1620.36,"Let Benjamin go."],[1624.08,"So what is this?"],[1626.4,"This is the exact reverse of what they did to him."],[1632.32,"They sold Joseph into slavery."],[1636.58,"And now they're there saying, no, no, no, no, no, it's slave us, but let him go."],[1643.46,"As angry as they might be about the favoritism, they're willing to do this rather than."],[1650.88,"Don't they say that you should take uh the one who had the cup as a slave too?"],[1658.16,"No, they're saying he's here too."],[1662.88,"He's here too."],[1664.32,"He came back."],[1665.2,"They didn't run away."],[1666.24,"Yeah. They didn't run away, he came back."],[1667.44,"Take us as slaves, let him go"],[1670.68,"Joseph says, No, I'm taking him as a slave, the rest of you go."],[1676.74,"And they can't go back without it."],[1679.54,"Well. They certainly could go back without Joseph."],[1685.06,"Well, yeah. Yeah."],[1686.34,"Yeah. So verse 18."],[1690.42,"Then Judah came near to him and said, So Judah comes up to him one on one."],[1697.5,"Oh my Lord, let your servant speak a word in my Lord's hearing."],[1701.02,"And do not let your anger burn against your servant, for you are even like Pharaoh."],[1706.56,"So he says, We know you're when you speak, it's the fair, it's Pharaoh speaking speaking, it's the king."],[1710.16,"Please hear me out"],[1711.5,"So, but please don't be angry at me."],[1715.42,"My Lord asked his servants, saying, Have you a father or a brother?"],[1719.5,"Then we said to my lord, We have a father, an old man, and a child of his old age, who is young, his brother is dead, and he alone is left of his mother's children, and his father loves him."],[1731.34,"Then you said to your servants, Bring him down to me that I may set my eyes on him."],[1736.14,"But we said to my Lord, the lad cannot leave his father, for if he should leave his father, his father would die."],[1743.98,"So he says, Look, we told you this before, like he's the last son of his mother."],[1751.66,"His father cannot handle this."],[1753.2,"But we say it' truse."],[1754.4,"Not mercy on himself"],[1754.94,"He's just asking for mercy."],[1760.83,"Mercy on his brother and his father."],[1769.31,"But you said to your servants, unless your youngest brother comes down with you, you shall see my face no more."],[1774.83,"So it was when we went up to your servant, my father, that we told him the words of my Lord."],[1779.87,"And our father said, Go back and buy us a little food."],[1783.31,"But we said, We cannot go down."],[1785.15,"If our youngest brother is with us, then we will go down, for we may not see the man's face unless our younger brother is with us."],[1792.75,"Then your servant our father said to us, You know, my wife bore me two sons, and the one went out from me, and I said, Surely he was eaten by a wild animal, and I have not seen him since."],[1803.99,"But if you take this one also from me and calamity befalls him, you shall bring down my gray hair with sorrow to the grave."],[1811.51,"Now therefore, when I come to your servant our father, and the lad is not with us, since his life is bound up in the lad's life, it will happen when he sees the lad is not with us, he will die."],[1822.55,"So your servants will bring down the gray hair of your servant our father with sorrow to the grave."],[1828.87,"So he says, Look, he's gonna, he's gonna die."],[1831.67,"He's gonna pine to death, he's gonna kill himself."],[1833.91,"I he's verse 32 For your servant became surety for the lad to my father, saying, If I do not bring him back to you, then I shall bear the blame before my father all my days."],[1843.35,"I So he's saying, Judas saying, myself guaranteed to my father that I would bring him back."],[1854.51,"Now therefore, let your servant remain instead of the lad as a servant to my Lord, and let the lad go up with his brothers."],[1861.63,"For how shall I go up to my father if the lad is not with me?"],[1865.15,"Lest perhaps I see the evil that would come upon my father."],[1868.37,"So he says, Take me, let him go."],[1872.98,"Because if you don't let him go, I don't want to see that happen to my father."],[1878.26,"I couldn't bear to see it."],[1880.23,"Notice the flip."],[1881.51,"Yeah, this is the complete."],[1882.73,"This is the one who lied to his father about Joseph being dead."],[1885.53,"He's changed And despite his father's mourning, said nothing."],[1891.22,"The brothers have changed."],[1896.66,"Chapter 45, verse 1."],[1898.18,"Now Joseph could not restrain himself before all those who stood by him, and he cried out, Make everyone go out from me."],[1905.06,"So no one stood with him while Joseph made himself known to his brothers."],[1908.42,"So he throws everybody else out of the room."],[1910.98,"Except his brothers."],[1913.22,"Then he wept aloud, and the Egyptians and the house of Pharaoh heard it."],[1918.12,"So everybody here, they're like, What is going on?"],[1921.24,"Joseph then said to his brothers, I am Joseph."],[1924.12,"Does my father still live?"],[1926.12,"But his brothers could not answer him, for they were stunned in his presence."],[1929.32,"Because they haven't said Joseph's name to him"],[1930.56,"As you might imagine."],[1938.3,"So he all of a sudden says, I'm Joseph."],[1941.1,"Is my father still alive?"],[1942.3,"And they're like."],[1949.03,"So they came near."],[1950.79,"Then he said, I am Joseph, your brother, whom you sold into Egypt."],[1954.39,"Now therefore, do not be grieved or angry with yourselves, because you sold me here, for God sent me before you to save life."],[1963.91,"So not only is he forgiven them, he says, Listen, don't feel guilty about it of what you did to me."],[1971.83,"That's way beyond not wanting revenge"],[1976.65,"I don't think I've ever forgiven someone who has wronged me enough to not want them to feel bad about it at least a little."],[1986.09,"But it's also time to put God's, you know, the providence of God in this big picture."],[1994.33,"You know, because the story is a history, and there's yeah, and so he's able to see that picture."],[2002.01,"That's easy to see, but like I said, whatever you feel."],[2005.53,"I've never had someone wrong me this much."],[2009.45,"But if I'm honest, even the people I've forgiven who have done bad things to me, I kind of want them to feel bad about it at least."],[2015.97,"You may be a more forgiving person than me"],[2017.77,"I'm just being honest about myself."],[2029.21,"Now that it's less about him, more about the grander."],[2033.45,"But it takes a person to see that."],[2035.77,"It takes a certain type of person to say, I mean, he could say this."],[2038.81,"He could say, I see that God's plan was to bring me here so that I could now save your lives."],[2046.14,"But you should still kind of feel bad about what you did to me."],[2050.7,"Yeah. More than that, though, because when he says save life, he's not talking about just them, he's talking about all the people."],[2056.86,"All the Egyptians."],[2059.9,"Yeah, yeah, yeah."],[2060.3,"ah. Ye Yeah."],[2060.5,"Yeah. But you can see that and still kind of want your brothers to feel bad"],[2060.86,"Yeah. Or still be like, you know, you guys gonna say you're sorry now?"],[2071.03,"But it seems like the dreams have something to do with that too."],[2075.99,"Yeah, yeah. Not yet."],[2077.67,"So he knows like if if the sh if the grain she's a found or something."],[2083.11,"Well his mother is departed though."],[2085.43,"But yeah. So I'm I'm just making the point that, he doesn't even want them to he doesn't even want them to feel bad about it."],[2093.05,"The people who wronged them."],[2094.25,"You're the one who talked about paths."],[2095.77,"Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah."],[2096.73,"Yeah, yeah. Yeah."],[2098.49,"Yeah. Well, he's gonna get more into that too."],[2100.49,"He's gonna get more into that too."],[2101.85,"I'm just making the point that this this is the level of his forgiveness."],[2106.13,"They still haven't asked for it."],[2110.85,"They still have not even asked for it."],[2113.65,"They have not apologized."],[2115.49,"They have not expressed any remorse."],[2117.17,"They have not admitted what they did to their brother."],[2120.53,"No, Judy can't lie because he said, My father said that he was killed by a wild animal."],[2126.59,"Like he they haven't come clean with anybody."],[2130.03,"They haven't confessed anything."],[2134.4,"That's he's he's not asking he is."],[2138.56,"This is ultimate forgiveness."],[2140.82,"This is. I'm not holding this against you at all."],[2144.18,"I don't even want you to feel bad about it."],[2147.06,"I'm not waiting. for you to apologize"],[2153.35,"And that's that's a that this is another image of forgiveness."],[2158.33,"Because I get these questions as a priest."],[2161.53,"Do I have to forgive someone who doesn't ask me for forgiveness?"],[2165.93,"Well. Do I have to forgive someone if they're not really sorry?"],[2176.48,"Saint Peter, how many times do I have to forgive my brother?"],[2181.76,"I mean, eventually I can stop."],[2183.54,"If they keep doing it."],[2187.31,"And because it's part of that pattern, right"],[2187.63,"This is the image before time of Christ's forgiveness."],[2187.75,"This is the image we have."],[2195.83,"So this is."],[2210.15,"Because he wanted to see how Benjamin was treated."],[2213.52,"He wanted to see."],[2214.56,"And he's not saying, I'm just gonna forget all this stuff ever happened."],[2219.53,"But what he's saying, and what forgiveness is, is his love for his brothers."],[2225.34,"When he saw them without Benjamin, without knowing what had happened to Benjamin, he wept."],[2232.34,"See, his brothers who had treated him that cruelly."],[2235.54,"Again, he wept."],[2238.92,"So his love for them, his love for his father, his love for Benjamin, is bigger than what they did to him."],[2245.96,"His love even for the people of Egypt."],[2249.13,"The other people of Canaan."],[2252.33,"The people of the other adjoining nations."],[2254.26,"And so this is why this is an image of Christ's forgiveness."],[2258.98,"Because Christ's forgiveness is not telling us, oh, it's no big deal."],[2264.58,"It's not saying I'm gonna forget this ever happened"],[2267.62,"But Christ's forgiveness is that the love of God is bigger."],[2271.38,"Much bigger, than any of these other things."],[2274.51,"And so Joseph is showing us an image of that."],[2278.77,"And what kind of forgiveness that is."],[2282.29,"Verse 6, for this is the second year of famine in the land, and five years still remain, in which there will be neither ploughing nor harvesting."],[2289.97,"For God sent me before you to preserve you as a remnant on the earth, and to sustain you as a great remnant."],[2297.33,"So now it was not you who sent me here, but God."],[2300.45,"And he made me a father to Pharaoh and Lord of all his house and ruler throughout all the land of Egypt."],[2309.65,"So there is, I'll pause here just briefly to say this is highly contested, like almost everything in Egyptian history now, but there is evidence that around this period there that where he says here, made me a father to Pharaoh, and you're like, that what you outrang Pharaoh?"],[2325.9,"But that that was actually a title."],[2330.06,"That was actually a title that could be given to a chief advisor of the king."],[2335.74,"Because as an advisor, it's father in more the spiritual father type of sense."],[2344.26,"What is it?"],[2344.82,"Osiris Ra type thing."],[2347.78,"Potentially, it's hard to say."],[2349.3,"Like I said, there's some evidence."],[2351.08,"And some of this is contested, and even if even if that is a thing, you get timeline stuff, and is that specifically what Joseph is referring to, or is he just saying this in a general sense?"],[2364.86,"All that enters into it."],[2367.42,"But it's worth mentioning that that was an idea."],[2373.42,"Hurry then and go up to my father and say to him, Thus says your son Joseph."],[2378.14,"Hopefully this won't shock him to death."],[2380.78,"Thus says your son Joseph, God made me Lord of all Egypt."],[2383.98,"Come down to me, do not tarry."],[2386.3,"You shall dwell in the land of Goshen, and you shall be near to me, you and your children, your children's children, your sheep and oxen, and all you have."],[2395.5,"There I will provide for you, lest you and your household and all you have come to poverty, for five years of famine still remain."],[2404.06,"The whole big extended household, bring them to Egypt"],[2404.66,"So he says, Go and tell him to bring the whole clan."],[2411.51,"Goshen that this is referring to is in the Delta."],[2414.95,"It's in the Nile Delta."],[2416.23,"So it's a particularly fertile region."],[2418.71,"It's a nice we have a nice place for you to settle."],[2421.67,"There's five years remaining."],[2423.19,"This whole running back and forth getting grain isn't going to work."],[2434.79,"And behold, your eyes, and the eyes of my brother Benjamin."],[2437.83,"see See it is my mouth that speaks to you."],[2441.45,"What is that?"],[2442.01,"That's again what he's going to tell his father."],[2444.67,"Because when he they show up and say, Joseph said this, he's going to be Joseph who got eaten by the ant."],[2449.07,"That's what he's gonna say"],[2452.21,"So he's saying to say to him, No, we, including Benjamin, we all saw Joseph."],[2456.93,"Joseph is alive, Joseph is in Egypt."],[2459.25,"This isn't a prank, or we're not hallucinating."],[2465.73,"Therefore, you shall tell my father of all my glory in Egypt, and of all you have seen, and you shall hurry and bring my father down here."],[2473.65,"Then he fell on his brother Benjamin's neck and wept."],[2476.61,"And Benjamin wept on his neck."],[2478.37,"Moreover, he kissed all his brothers and wept over them."],[2481.49,"And after that his brothers talked with him."],[2488.21,"So we see here there's this reconciliation."],[2491.11,"It's not just forgiveness, like Joseph forgives and moves on with his life."],[2495.47,"But there's this reconciliation."],[2498.68,"And like Esau, Joseph doesn't demand anything for that reconciliation."],[2507.96,"Doesn't demand some kind of recompense."],[2510.12,"Does it demand some kind of groveling?"],[2513.5,"Apologies, whatever. It's just given."],[2521.47,"Verse 16. Now the report of it was heard in Pharaoh's house, saying, Joseph's brothers have come."],[2526.59,"So it pleased Pharaoh and his servants well."],[2528.75,"So Pharaoh said to Joseph, Say to your brothers, do this, load your conveyances and depart."],[2534.11,"Go to the land of Canaan, bring your father and your households and come to me."],[2536.35,"I will give you the best of the land of Egypt, and you will eat the fat of the land"],[2543.03,"Now you are commanded, do this."],[2544.87,"Takes carts out of the land of Egypt for your little ones and your wives."],[2549.11,"Bring your father and come."],[2551.03,"Also do not be concerned about your goods, for the best of all the land of Egypt is yours."],[2556.65,"So Pharaoh hears about it and says, Yeah, whatever they need, he loves Joseph."],[2562.41,"Joseph's family is good with him."],[2564.67,"Bring everybody here."],[2567.55,"I'll help facilitate the move."],[2569.39,"That's what the whole thing about the carts is about."],[2571.4,"Because obviously little kids' wives can't necessarily make the trip on foot."],[2576.14,"So he's like, I'm gonna send stuff to help you make this move."],[2579.74,"Verse 21 Thus the sons of Israel did so, and Joseph gave them carts according to the command of Pharaoh, and he gave them provisions for the journey."],[2592.5,"He gave to all of them to each man two changes of garments, but to Benjamin he gave three hundred pieces of gold and five changes of exceptionally fine garments."],[2602.1,"He also sent to his father these things, ten donkeys loaded with the good things of Egypt, and ten mules loaded with grain, bread, and food for his father for the journey."],[2611.7,"So he sent his brothers away, and they departed, and he said to them, See that you do not become angry with each other along the way."],[2622.83,"Yeah. Talk about everything else"],[2623.67,"So see, Joseph has a sense of humor about the whole thing."],[2629.75,"Then they went up out of Egypt and came to the land of Canaan to Jacob their father."],[2634.15,"Thus they told him, saying, Joseph, your son, is still alive, and he is ruler over all the land of Egypt."],[2639.75,"But Jacob's mind was completely stunned, for he could not believe them."],[2644.71,"Remember the son who you thought was dead for the last twenty some odd years?"],[2649.35,"Yeah, he's alive, and he's the ruler of Egypt."],[2655.43,"Stunned, yeah. But when they told him all the words Joseph had said to them, and when he saw the carts Joseph had sent to carry him, the spirit of Jacob their father revived."],[2667.99,"But yeah, and that's what is the spirit of came back to life"],[2668.51,"I shouldn't think so."],[2674.95,"They were so worried he was going to go down into his grave if something happened to Benjamin, but now he comes back to life."],[2682.23,"Then Israel said, It is a great thing to me that my son Joseph is still alive."],[2686.87,"I will go and see him before I die."],[2690.39,"So time-wise, this is where we'll leave off."],[2694.23,"Um we will probably, the next time we get together, which may not be next week, we may well finish Genesis."],[2706.39,"Or we may not."],[2707.43,"Maybe two more Bible studies."],[2708.79,"We'll see. One or two more Bible studies will be done with Genesis, and then we'll get into Exodus."],[2712.39,"'ll But so for now, I turn off the recording."],[2712.71,"Thank you, everybody"],[2720.11,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the whole counsel of God."],[2727.47,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2732.83,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":21.44,"lv":2,"h":"Genesis 43:1-5 - Back to Egypt?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Famine severe</b> - grain from Egypt eaten</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>7-year famine</b>; animals starving too</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Simeon left</b> behind all this time - Jacob's decision: \"<b>Bye, Simeon</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Jacob: \"go back and buy us a <b>little food</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Judah</b> speaks: man warned \"<b>You shall not see my face unless your brother is with you</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">send <b>Benjamin</b> → we go; if not, <b>we won't go</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Judah: \"he will <b>kill us</b>\" - implied: \"I know you don't care, Dad. <b>But I do</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":103.25,"lv":3,"h":"43:6-7: Why did you tell him?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Israel</b> (= Jacob): \"Why did you deal so <b>wrongfully</b> with me\" - telling him of <b>another brother</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Brothers: man asked <b>pointedly</b> about family - \"Is your father alive? Have you another brother?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"Could we possibly have known he would say, <b>bring your brother down</b>?\"</li></ul>"},{"t":149.15,"lv":3,"h":"Jacob vs. Israel","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: why the shift from <b>Jacob</b> to <b>Israel</b>?</li><li class=\"d0\">Not just translation - he has <b>both names</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Abraham: name changed, <b>just Abraham</b> after; here it <b>goes back and forth</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Usually \"<b>Israel</b>\" = point about the <b>people, his descendants</b> as a whole</li><li class=\"d1\">Genesis = <b>prologue to the Torah</b></li><li class=\"d1\">named after the <b>wrestling match</b>: \"the one who <b>struggles with God</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">that's the <b>character of Israel</b> going forward</li></ul>"},{"t":221.56,"lv":3,"h":"Withholding vs. Abraham","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Contrast with <b>Abraham</b>: he offered the <b>most precious thing</b> to God</li><li class=\"d0\">Jacob now <b>withholds</b> the most precious thing</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Bickering, infighting</b> even between the tribes</li><li class=\"d0\">Who's talking to him? <b>Judah</b></li><li class=\"d1\">enmity <b>Judah / Israel</b> prefigures the <b>kingdoms splitting</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Judah = the one <b>talking sense, speaking truth</b>; Israel <b>withholds</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Re-emphasizes the <b>wrestling</b> - to descendants: \"this is where you come from\" - \"<b>apple doesn't fall far from the tree</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":304.46,"lv":2,"h":"43:8-14 - Judah's surety, Jacob's gifts","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Judah: \"<b>send the lad with me</b>... that we may live and not die\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Reuben</b> tried the same (\"trust me\") - <b>Judah</b>: if we don't go, <b>everyone dies of starvation</b>, Benjamin too</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>v. 9</b>: \"I myself will be <b>surety</b> for him... let me <b>bear the blame</b> all my days\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Adds: if you'd let us go the first time, <b>we'd have been back twice</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>v. 11</b>: \"If it must be so\" - take <b>a present</b>: balm, honey, spices, myrrh, pistachios, almonds</li><li class=\"d1\">not foodstuffs for herds - <b>tree resin</b> etc. → \"<b>ingratiate yourselves</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Take <b>double money</b> + the money returned in the sacks: \"perhaps an <b>oversight</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"May God give you grace before the man\" - release <b>Simeon</b> and Benjamin</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>If I am bereaved, I am bereaved</b>\" - same strategy as <b>meeting Esau</b>: gifts to ingratiate</li><li class=\"d1\">less to give in famine; but <b>sees the sense</b> of Judah - \"if we don't try, we're all dead\"</li></ul>"},{"t":481.99,"lv":2,"h":"43:15-17 - Joseph sees Benjamin","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Men take present, Benjamin, double money → <b>stood before Joseph</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Joseph sees <b>Benjamin</b>, \"his brother by the same mother\" → tells steward: slaughter an animal, \"<b>dine with me at noon</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Brothers brought to <b>Joseph's house</b></li></ul>"},{"t":532.19,"lv":3,"h":"Why he wanted Benjamin intact","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Joseph knew <b>what his dad was like</b> - with Joseph gone, <b>Benjamin = favorite</b></li><li class=\"d1\">youngest son as favorite <b>almost got Joseph killed</b></li><li class=\"d1\">reason to think they'd <b>killed Benjamin too</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Wanted to see him <b>intact</b> → conclusion: \"my dad may not have changed, but <b>something had changed with his brothers</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Repentant people → <b>forgiveness easier</b>; but he'd <b>already forgiven</b> them</li></ul>"},{"t":597.45,"lv":3,"h":"Joseph vs. revenge stories","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Esau's forgiveness was a big deal - but Jacob <b>didn't try to murder Esau</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Joseph: <b>sold into slavery</b>, <b>years in prison</b> - \"if anybody had reason not to forgive\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Aside: movie <b>Gladiator</b> - classic <b>revenge story</b></li><li class=\"d1\">plays back to <b>Greek tragedies</b> - wronged man <b>wreaks horrible revenge</b>; we find it <b>satisfying</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Not what Genesis gives us</b> - satisfying endings:</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Jacob and Esau reconciled</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Isaac and Ishmael</b> bury their father together</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Joseph forgives</b> his brothers - they <b>haven't asked</b>, don't know who he is</li><li class=\"d0\">Couldn't even keep them imprisoned <b>more than three days</b> - part of <b>the pattern</b></li></ul>"},{"t":712.78,"lv":3,"h":"Christ's blood speaks a better word","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Christ's resurrection</b> - no revenge on <b>Jerusalem</b> or the <b>Romans</b>; rises <b>bringing forgiveness</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Hebrews</b>: blood of Christ speaks <b>a better word than Abel</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Abel's blood</b> cried from the ground for <b>justice</b>; Christ's calls out for <b>forgiveness</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Joseph = part of <b>establishing that pattern</b>: Jacob/Esau, Isaac/Ishmael</li><li class=\"d0\">Forgiveness and reconciliation <b>not a New Testament thing</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not \"<b>mean angry God of vengeance</b>\" in OT, then Jesus brings forgiveness</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>earliest pattern</b> in the Bible of <b>the good ending</b> - \"<b>not vengeance</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":805.17,"lv":2,"h":"43:18-25 - Afraid at Joseph's house","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Brothers <b>afraid</b> - brought to the house, nobody's told them why</li><li class=\"d1\">a <b>huge palatial</b> house by the day's standards</li><li class=\"d0\">Think: it's the <b>money in the sacks</b> → \"make a case against us\" → <b>take us as slaves</b> with our donkeys</li><li class=\"d0\">Talk to the <b>steward</b> at the door: found money \"in <b>full weight</b>\" - brought it back, plus more</li><li class=\"d1\">weight, not <b>coins</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"that whole money thing was a <b>misunderstanding</b>... don't enslave us, maybe\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Steward: \"<b>Mercy be on you, do not be afraid</b>\" - \"<b>your God</b>... has given you treasure\"; got your payment</li><li class=\"d0\">Brings <b>Simeon</b> out to them → now <b>confused</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Water, feet washed, donkeys fed; present readied for <b>noon</b></li></ul>"},{"t":955.58,"lv":2,"h":"43:26-31 - Bowing, and Joseph weeps","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Present brought in; <b>bow to the earth</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Joseph: \"Is your <b>father well</b>? ... still alive?\" - \"Blessed be that man in God\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Bow again</b></li><li class=\"d1\">aside: \"<b>not worshiping Joseph</b>\" - bowing/prostrating ≠ worship (\"don't know who needs to hear that\")</li><li class=\"d0\">To Benjamin: \"May God grant you mercy, <b>my son</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Heart yearned</b> → seeks somewhere to <b>weep</b>, inner chamber; washes face: \"<b>Serve the bread</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"Joseph doesn't have a <b>super good poker face</b>\" - keeps stepping away</li></ul>"},{"t":1043.47,"lv":2,"h":"43:32-34 - Seating and portions","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Three tables: <b>Joseph</b> alone, <b>brothers</b>, <b>Egyptians</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Egyptians <b>can't eat with Hebrews</b> - \"an abomination\" (the <b>hygiene</b> thing)</li><li class=\"d1\">Joseph at the <b>head table</b> - \"the big cheese\"; following Egyptian rules</li><li class=\"d0\">Brothers seated <b>oldest to youngest</b> - they look at each other <b>astonished</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Benjamin's portion five times</b> as much</li><li class=\"d0\">They <b>drank and were merry</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1135.27,"lv":3,"h":"How food flowed down a table","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Official's food from kitchen → <b>he takes what he wants</b>, sends rest to other tables</li><li class=\"d1\">Egyptians first, then the <b>leftovers</b> - <b>descending order</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Sending directly <b>from his table to the brothers</b> = weird; to <b>Benjamin</b>, the youngest = weirder</li><li class=\"d0\">Same in <b>families</b>: food to <b>father</b> → firstborn son → down the sons → <b>mom</b> → daughters</li><li class=\"d1\">Jacob's house likely <b>leapfrogging</b>: him, <b>Joseph</b> - \"part of the problem\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Hierarchy <b>reinforced every meal</b> - not just occasional favoritism (\"my sisters know I'm the favorite\")</li><li class=\"d1\">source of the brothers' <b>rage</b>: \"thrown in their face day in and day out\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1284.24,"lv":3,"h":"A test of the brothers","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Brothers: \"why did he want to see our youngest brother so bad? Why is he <b>spoiling him</b>?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Q: isn't he <b>reestablishing order</b> by lining them up? - yes, <b>then violating it</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Perhaps a <b>subtle clue</b> he knows what's going on</li><li class=\"d0\">Purpose: <b>a test</b> - he hasn't told them who he is</li><li class=\"d1\">will they get <b>angry</b>? <b>object</b> to the youngest being favored?</li></ul>"},{"t":1332.19,"lv":2,"h":"Genesis 44:1-5 - The silver cup","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Fill sacks with food; <b>money back</b> in each sack</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Silver cup</b> (very valuable) from the house where they just ate → into <b>youngest's sack</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Morning: sent away; not far from the city → steward: \"<b>Why have you repaid evil for good?</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">cup \"with which he indeed practices <b>divination</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Divination: keeps up the ruse he's <b>Egyptian</b></li><li class=\"d1\">read the <b>dregs of the wine</b> for <b>omens</b> - like tea leaves</li></ul>"},{"t":1436.15,"lv":2,"h":"44:6-13 - Cup found in Benjamin's sack","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Brothers: \"<b>Far be it from us</b>\" - we <b>brought back</b> the money from Canaan</li><li class=\"d1\">\"if we were dishonest, we wouldn't have brought it back\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"With whomever it is found, let him <b>die</b>, and we also will be my lord's <b>servants</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Steward: \"as you say\" - finder shall be <b>my servant</b>, rest <b>blameless</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not killing - <b>slavery for theft</b>: work off the value of what you stole</li><li class=\"d1\">for a silver cup, <b>a long time</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Searched oldest first, youngest last → cup in <b>Benjamin's sack</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Tore clothes</b>; loaded donkeys; <b>returned to the city</b> - not home</li><li class=\"d1\">can't go back to their dad <b>without Benjamin</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1569.86,"lv":2,"h":"44:14-17 - Reverse of Joseph's sale","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Judah and brothers at Joseph's house, <b>fall on the ground</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Joseph: \"such a man as I can certainly practice <b>divination</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Judah: \"How shall we <b>clear ourselves</b>? <b>God has found out</b> the wrongdoing\" - \"here we are, <b>slaves</b>, both we and he\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Joseph: \"<b>Far be it from me</b>\" - only the one with the cup stays; \"go up <b>in peace</b> to your father\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Exact reverse</b> of what they did: <b>sold Joseph into slavery</b> → now \"<b>slave us, but let him go</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">as angry as they were about <b>favoritism</b></li><li class=\"d0\">They <b>could</b> go back without Benjamin - but won't</li></ul>"},{"t":1686.34,"lv":2,"h":"44:18-34 - Judah's plea","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>v. 18</b>: Judah comes <b>one on one</b>; \"do not let your anger burn... you are even like <b>Pharaoh</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Recounts: <b>old father</b>, child of his old age; \"his brother is dead\"; \"his father <b>loves him</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"the lad cannot leave his father, or his father would <b>die</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Asks <b>mercy for his brother and father</b>, not himself</li><li class=\"d0\">Jacob's words: \"my wife bore me <b>two sons</b>... surely eaten by a wild animal\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"bring down my <b>gray hair with sorrow to the grave</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">his life \"<b>bound up in the lad's life</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>v. 32</b>: Judah <b>surety</b> to his father - \"bear the blame all my days\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Let your servant <b>remain instead of the lad</b>\" - \"how shall I go up if the lad is not with me?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"I couldn't <b>bear to see it</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1880.23,"lv":3,"h":"Judah has changed","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Notice the <b>flip</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">This is the one who <b>lied to his father</b> about Joseph being dead</li><li class=\"d1\">despite his father's mourning, <b>said nothing</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>The brothers have changed</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1896.66,"lv":2,"h":"Genesis 45:1-4 - I am Joseph","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Joseph <b>can't restrain himself</b> - \"<b>Make everyone go out</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Throws everyone out <b>except the brothers</b>; weeps <b>aloud</b> - Egyptians and Pharaoh's house <b>hear it</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>I am Joseph.</b> Does my father still live?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Brothers <b>can't answer</b> - stunned</li><li class=\"d1\">they never said <b>Joseph's name</b> to him</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Come near... I am Joseph, your brother, whom <b>you sold into Egypt</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1963.91,"lv":3,"h":"Don't feel guilty: God sent me","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"do not be <b>grieved or angry with yourselves</b>... <b>God sent me</b> before you to <b>save life</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Beyond not wanting revenge - he doesn't even want them to <b>feel bad</b></li><li class=\"d1\">speaker's honesty: even forgiven people, \"I kind of want them to <b>feel bad</b> at least\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Takes seeing <b>God's providence</b> in the big picture; <b>save life</b> = Egyptians and all the people, not just them</li><li class=\"d0\">Discussion: still want them to <b>say sorry</b>? - he <b>doesn't wait</b> for it</li><li class=\"d0\">Brothers have <b>not asked</b>, <b>not apologized</b>, <b>not confessed</b> to anybody</li><li class=\"d1\">Judah can't lie: father was told \"<b>killed by a wild animal</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2153.35,"lv":3,"h":"Forgiveness as an image of Christ","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Ultimate forgiveness</b>: \"not holding this against you... <b>not waiting for you to apologize</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Priest's questions: <b>do I have to forgive</b> someone who doesn't ask? isn't sorry?</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>St. Peter</b>: how many times? - \"eventually I can stop\"?</li><li class=\"d0\">This is \"<b>the image before the time of Christ's forgiveness</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Not \"forget it ever happened\" - forgiveness = <b>his love for his brothers</b></li><li class=\"d1\">wept without knowing what happened to <b>Benjamin</b>; wept seeing cruel brothers</li><li class=\"d1\">love for <b>father</b>, <b>Benjamin</b>, <b>Egypt</b>, <b>Canaan</b>, adjoining nations - <b>bigger than what they did</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Christ's forgiveness not \"<b>no big deal</b>\" - <b>the love of God is bigger</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2282.29,"lv":2,"h":"45:6-8 - Preserved as a remnant","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>2nd year of famine</b>, <b>5 years</b> remain - no ploughing or harvest</li><li class=\"d0\">\"God sent me before you to preserve you as a <b>remnant</b>... <b>great remnant</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Not you who sent me here, but God</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Father to Pharaoh</b>, Lord of all his house, ruler of Egypt\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>highly contested</b> like most Egyptian history - evidence it was a <b>title</b> for a <b>chief advisor</b> of the king</li><li class=\"d1\">\"father\" in the <b>spiritual father</b> sense - Osiris/Ra type thing? - hard to say</li><li class=\"d1\">timeline questions - maybe general sense; \"worth mentioning\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2373.42,"lv":2,"h":"45:9-15 - Come to Goshen","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Hurry... go up to my father: <b>Thus says your son Joseph</b>\" (\"hopefully this won't shock him to death\")</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Come down to me</b>, do not tarry\" - dwell in <b>Goshen</b>, near me - children, flocks, all you have</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Nile Delta</b> - <b>fertile</b> region</li><li class=\"d1\">5 years left - <b>running back and forth</b> for grain won't work</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Your eyes, and <b>Benjamin's eyes</b>, see it is my mouth that speaks\"</li><li class=\"d1\">answer for Jacob's doubt: we all saw him - \"<b>not a prank, not hallucinating</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Tell my father of <b>all my glory in Egypt</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Falls on <b>Benjamin's neck</b>, weeps; kisses <b>all his brothers</b>; then they talk</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Reconciliation</b>, not just forgiveness-and-move-on</li><li class=\"d1\">like <b>Esau</b>, demands <b>no recompense</b>, no <b>groveling</b> - \"it's just given\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2521.47,"lv":2,"h":"45:16-24 - Pharaoh's invitation","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Pharaoh's house hears: \"Joseph's brothers have come\" - <b>pleased</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Pharaoh: load up, go to <b>Canaan</b>, bring father and households</li><li class=\"d1\">\"the <b>best of the land of Egypt</b>... eat the <b>fat of the land</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Carts</b> for little ones and wives - leave goods behind</li><li class=\"d1\">he loves Joseph; \"I'll help facilitate the move\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Joseph gives carts, provisions; <b>two changes of garments</b> each</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Benjamin</b>: <b>300 pieces of gold</b>, <b>5 changes</b> of fine garments</li><li class=\"d0\">Sends father <b>10 donkeys</b> of Egypt's good things, <b>10 mules</b> of grain, bread</li><li class=\"d0\">Parting: \"<b>See that you do not become angry with each other</b> along the way\" - \"Joseph has a <b>sense of humor</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2629.75,"lv":2,"h":"45:25-28 - Jacob revived","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Back in Canaan: \"<b>Joseph is still alive</b>, ruler over all Egypt\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Jacob <b>stunned</b>, couldn't believe - son thought dead <b>twenty-some years</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Hears Joseph's words, sees the <b>carts</b> → \"<b>spirit of Jacob revived</b>\" - came back to life</li><li class=\"d1\">he'd been ready to go to the <b>grave</b> over Benjamin</li><li class=\"d0\">Israel: \"a great thing... Joseph is alive. <b>I will go and see him before I die</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2690.39,"lv":3,"h":"Wrap-up","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Time to stop here</li><li class=\"d0\">Next time (maybe <b>not next week</b>): may <b>finish Genesis</b> - or <b>one or two more</b> studies</li><li class=\"d0\">Then <b>Exodus</b></li></ul>"}],"next":"Next time (maybe not next week): <b>finish Genesis</b> in one or two more studies, then <b>Exodus</b>"});
